                <pb facs="0582" n="510" xml:id="pg510"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 17147/1.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Portuguese Minister to the Secretary of
                        State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Portuguese Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1909-05-01"><hi rendition="#italic">May 1,
                        1909</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of April 30, 1909, giving through me to the Government of Portugal
                    formal notice on behalf of the United States of the intended termination of the
                    commercial agreements concluded between the two countries on May 22, 1899, and
                    November 19, 1902.</p>
                <p>A copy of your note has already been forwarded to his majesty’s Government.</p>
                <p>I avail, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alte.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
